# What must never reach the frontend image's build context.
#
# node_modules is the one that matters. The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and then
# `COPY . .`, so without this rule the host's node_modules is copied straight
# over the one just installed inside the container. On a Windows host that
# replaces Linux binaries with Windows ones — esbuild and rollup both ship a
# platform-specific executable — and the build fails, or worse, succeeds
# against the wrong toolchain.
#
# dist is excluded for a quieter reason: a stale local build would be copied in
# and then overwritten by `npm run build`, which wastes transfer and makes the
# image's provenance ambiguous if the build step is ever skipped.

node_modules/
dist/

.git/
.gitignore

# Vite inlines any VITE_-prefixed variable into the bundle at build time, so a
# local .env here would end up readable in the shipped JavaScript. The image
# takes its configuration from build args instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
coverage/
